      {
        "id": 21506,
        "name": "lynkfox",
        "username": "lynkfox",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/{size}/1997_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-16T22:43:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>we have jumped back and forth. Given that we still cannot get a good (semi) reliable win on many villians, we have stuck to regular mode, except for occasionally - We hit up Advanced Baron Blade the other night for a change of pace and made the game a lot more fun than baron blade usually is - For us, he's trounced so easily now that we know the decks the added challenge was a nice touch.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thats our general look on advanced. We play to have fun, and winning (or a terrible complete destruction as we had the other night against Citizen Dawn. The citizen that reduces damage to all citizens by 1 plus the one that states all other citizens can't be hurt and damage done to him is reduced by one... having to do a minimal of 3 damage to him to even start to hurt him... ouch!) but occasionally winning becomes way to easy, and thats where advance mode comes in for an added bit of challenge ... when the time is right</p>",
