      {
        "id": 21508,
        "name": "LCinn",
        "username": "LCinn",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lcinn/{size}/2659_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-17T11:26:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I haven't played Advanced Mode yet, but from looking at the villains, I get the impression that sometimes advanced mode adds something more than just difficulty, and sometimes it's just much harder. For example, The Ennead is very unlikely to flip on normal, so advanced would actually add something more than just difficulty. Same for Akash'butha, where her sides don't really feel that much different on normal, while on advanced, you finally know why she's glowing red with lava on her flip side. I really like this. I'm not so sure if the ones that are just harder, like (once again, these are just impressions, I haven't actually played any of these and will play all of these eventually) Grand Warlord Voss, are for me. But even then it's obviously great the higher difficulty exists for those who do want it.</p>",
