      {
        "id": 21517,
        "name": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "username": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/da6949/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-19T12:40:01.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"arenson9\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/48/1900_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> arenson9:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>TheSoundOfTrees wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;Edit : I just wrote in another thread that, for me, it feels like the Rook City villains are as difficult in Normal than other Villains in advanced - like if they were not really balanced in the same way than other Villains before and after.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;Wouldn't you expect that, given their difficulty levels? The core game levels are 1, 1, 3, 3, while the RC villains are 2, 2, 4, 4.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Spite and Plague Rat may be rated 2, but I don't think they are in the same difficulty category as other 2s, or even 3s, on non advanced.</p>",
